(window.STEP_DATA = window.STEP_DATA || {})[16] = {"n":16,"set":"B","level":"Intermediate","band":"B1 50% · B2 50%","sec":[{"id":"R","name":"Reading Comprehension","ar":"فهم المقروء","min":70,"from":1,"to":40,"g":[{"t":"How lightning works","p":["Lightning is one of the most spectacular and dangerous natural events on Earth. At any given moment, around two thousand thunderstorms are taking place around the world, producing roughly one hundred flashes of lightning every second. A single bolt can heat the air around it to about thirty thousand degrees Celsius, five times hotter than the surface of the sun. Yet although lightning has fascinated and frightened people for thousands of years, scientists still do not fully understand how it begins.","Lightning is produced inside tall storm clouds called cumulonimbus clouds. These clouds contain strong upward and downward currents of air, as well as water droplets, ice crystals and soft pellets of ice called graupel. As these particles move up and down and collide with each other, electric charges are separated. Smaller, lighter ice crystals, which usually carry a positive charge, are carried to the top of the cloud, while heavier graupel, which tends to carry a negative charge, collects in the middle and lower parts.","When the difference in charge becomes large enough, the air, which normally does not conduct electricity well, can no longer act as an insulator. A path of electrically charged air, called a 'stepped leader', begins to move downwards from the cloud in a series of short jumps. As it approaches the ground, positive charges rise to meet it from tall objects such as trees, towers and buildings. When the two meet, a powerful electric current flows along the path. This is the bright flash we see, known as the return stroke. It all happens in a fraction of a second.","Thunder is the sound produced by lightning. The extreme heat causes the air to expand so quickly that it creates a shock wave, which we hear as a loud crack or a long rumble. Because light travels much faster than sound, we see lightning before we hear thunder. Counting the seconds between the flash and the thunder and dividing by three gives a rough idea of the distance of the storm in kilometres.","Lightning can strike the same place more than once, despite the popular saying. Tall buildings, such as the Burj Khalifa in Dubai, are struck many times every year. They are protected by lightning rods, metal rods connected to the ground by thick cables, which carry the electric current safely into the earth.","Each year, lightning kills thousands of people worldwide. Experts advise that when thunder can be heard, people should go indoors or into a car with a metal roof. They should avoid open fields, hilltops, isolated trees and water. Although lightning is dangerous, it also plays a useful role in nature: it helps to convert nitrogen in the air into forms that plants can use as nutrients."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"What is the passage mainly about?","o":["the history of weather forecasting","how lightning forms and how to stay safe","how to build tall buildings","the climate of Dubai"],"k":1,"ty":"main idea","e":"The passage explains lightning, thunder and safety.","h":"تكوّن البرق والسلامة منه."},{"n":2,"s":"According to paragraph 1, what do scientists still not fully understand?","o":["how lightning begins","why storms are dangerous","how hot lightning is","where storms occur"],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"'scientists still do not fully understand how it begins'.","h":"كيف يبدأ البرق."},{"n":3,"s":"How are electric charges separated inside storm clouds?","o":["Moving particles collide with each other.","The sun heats the cloud unevenly.","Lightning rods pull them apart.","Rain falls from the top of the cloud."],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 2 explains this.","h":"تصادم الجسيمات."},{"n":4,"s":"Where does negatively charged graupel usually collect?","o":["at the very top of the cloud","on the ground","outside the cloud","in the middle and lower parts of the cloud"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 2 says so.","h":"الوسط والأسفل."},{"n":5,"s":"The word 'insulator' in paragraph 3 refers to something that","o":["produces electricity","stores rainwater","does not allow electricity to pass easily","measures temperature"],"k":2,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Air normally does not conduct electricity well.","h":"عازل."},{"n":6,"s":"What is the 'return stroke'?","o":["the first downward jump of charge","the sound of thunder","the bright flash when the two paths meet","a metal rod on a building"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 3 defines it.","h":"الوميض الساطع."},{"n":7,"s":"Why do we see lightning before we hear thunder?","o":["Thunder starts later than lightning.","Our eyes are more sensitive than our ears.","Thunder is produced far away.","Light travels much faster than sound."],"k":3,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 4 explains this.","h":"الضوء أسرع من الصوت."},{"n":8,"s":"If the thunder comes nine seconds after the flash, the storm is about","o":["nine kilometres away","three kilometres away","one kilometre away","twenty-seven kilometres away"],"k":1,"ty":"inference","e":"Seconds divided by three = kilometres.","h":"ثلاثة كيلومترات."},{"n":9,"s":"Why does the writer mention the Burj Khalifa?","o":["to describe the tallest building's design","to explain how thunder is produced","to show that lightning can strike the same place many times","to show that buildings cause storms"],"k":2,"ty":"purpose","e":"It is struck many times a year.","h":"البرق يضرب المكان نفسه."},{"n":10,"s":"Which of the following is NOT recommended during a thunderstorm?","o":["going indoors","sitting in a car with a metal roof","standing under an isolated tree","avoiding open fields"],"k":2,"ty":"NOT / EXCEPT","e":"People should avoid isolated trees.","h":"الوقوف تحت شجرة منفردة."}]},{"t":"The economics of airlines","p":["Flying has never been more popular, and for many people it has become a normal part of life. Before the pandemic in 2020, more than four billion passengers travelled by air each year. Yet despite this huge demand, running an airline is one of the most difficult businesses in the world. Profit margins are often very small, and many well-known airlines have gone bankrupt over the years.","One reason is that airlines have extremely high costs. Aircraft are very expensive: a new long-distance jet can cost hundreds of millions of dollars. Airlines must also pay for fuel, crew salaries, maintenance, airport fees and insurance. Fuel alone can account for around a quarter of an airline's costs, and its price can change suddenly because of global events, making planning difficult.","At the same time, competition is fierce. On many routes, several airlines compete for the same passengers, and customers can compare prices online in seconds. Because a seat on a plane is a 'perishable' product, like fresh fruit, airlines have a strong incentive to fill every seat. Once a plane takes off, an empty seat earns nothing.","To deal with this, airlines use a system called yield management or dynamic pricing. Computer programs constantly adjust ticket prices according to demand, the time before departure and the number of seats still available. This is why two passengers sitting next to each other may have paid very different prices. Business travellers who book at the last minute usually pay much more than holiday makers who book months in advance.","Low-cost airlines have changed the industry by reducing costs wherever possible. They often use only one type of aircraft to simplify maintenance and training, fly to smaller airports with lower fees and keep their planes in the air for more hours each day. They also charge extra for services that traditional airlines once included, such as checked baggage, seat selection and meals. These 'ancillary revenues' can make up a significant share of their income.","Airlines also face growing pressure to reduce their environmental impact, as aviation is responsible for a notable share of global carbon emissions. Companies are investing in more fuel-efficient aircraft and exploring sustainable aviation fuels, but these solutions are expensive. In Saudi Arabia, the aviation sector is expanding rapidly, with new airlines and airports planned to support tourism and connect the Kingdom with the world. Balancing growth, profitability and sustainability will be the industry's greatest challenge in the coming decades."],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"What is the main idea of the passage?","o":["Flying is becoming less popular.","All airlines make large profits.","Fuel is cheap and easy to obtain.","Running an airline is financially very challenging."],"k":3,"ty":"main idea","e":"Despite demand, airlines struggle to make profits.","h":"إدارة الطيران صعبة ماليًا."},{"n":12,"s":"Why is fuel a particular problem for airlines?","o":["It is used only on long flights.","Its price can change suddenly.","It is cheaper than salaries.","It is not available at small airports."],"k":1,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 2 explains this.","h":"تقلب السعر."},{"n":13,"s":"Why does the writer compare an airline seat to fresh fruit?","o":["Both are sold in markets.","Both lose their value if they are not sold in time.","Both are cheap.","Both are healthy."],"k":1,"ty":"purpose","e":"Once a plane takes off, an empty seat earns nothing.","h":"تفقد قيمتها إن لم تُبع."},{"n":14,"s":"The word 'incentive' in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to","o":["fear","rule","reason to do something","difficulty"],"k":2,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Airlines have a strong reason to fill every seat.","h":"حافز."},{"n":15,"s":"What is dynamic pricing?","o":["charging the same price for all seats","changing ticket prices according to demand and timing","giving free tickets to frequent flyers","selling food on board"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 4 explains it.","h":"تغيير الأسعار حسب الطلب."},{"n":16,"s":"Who usually pays the most for tickets?","o":["holiday makers who book early","children","passengers on low-cost airlines","business travellers who book at the last minute"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 4 says so.","h":"رجال الأعمال المتأخرون في الحجز."},{"n":17,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a way low-cost airlines reduce costs?","o":["using one type of aircraft","flying to smaller airports","paying pilots lower salaries","keeping planes in the air longer"],"k":2,"ty":"NOT / EXCEPT","e":"Salaries are not mentioned.","h":"الرواتب غير مذكورة."},{"n":18,"s":"What are 'ancillary revenues'?","o":["income from extra services such as baggage and meals","money from ticket sales","government support","profits from fuel sales"],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 5 explains this.","h":"إيرادات الخدمات الإضافية."},{"n":19,"s":"Why are solutions to aviation's environmental impact difficult?","o":["They are expensive.","Passengers do not care about the environment.","Aircraft cannot use new fuels.","Governments have banned them."],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"'these solutions are expensive'.","h":"مكلفة."},{"n":20,"s":"What does the writer suggest about the future of the airline industry?","o":["It will stop growing.","Low-cost airlines will disappear.","It must balance growth, profit and sustainability.","Fuel prices will fall permanently."],"k":2,"ty":"summary / conclusion","e":"The last sentence states the challenge.","h":"الموازنة بين النمو والربح والاستدامة."}]},{"t":"The legend of the Hanging Gardens of Babylon","p":["Of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World, the Hanging Gardens of Babylon are perhaps the most mysterious. Ancient writers described a magnificent series of terraced gardens filled with trees, flowers and flowing water, rising high above the dry plains of Mesopotamia. Yet unlike the Great Pyramid of Giza, which still stands, no trace of the gardens has ever been definitely found. Some historians even doubt that they existed at all.","According to the most famous version of the story, the gardens were built in the sixth century BCE by King Nebuchadnezzar II of Babylon, in what is now Iraq. He is said to have created them for his wife, Amytis, who came from a green, mountainous region and missed the landscapes of her homeland. The gardens were described as rising in layers, like the seats of a theatre, supported by strong arches and walls.","The descriptions also mention a remarkable irrigation system. Water had to be lifted from the River Euphrates to the top of the gardens and then allowed to flow down through the terraces. Some ancient writers suggested that machines with screws or chains of buckets were used. If this is true, it would have been an extraordinary engineering achievement for its time.","However, there are serious problems with this story. None of the surviving Babylonian records from Nebuchadnezzar's time mention the gardens, even though they describe his palaces and other building projects in detail. The Greek historian Herodotus, who wrote a long description of Babylon in the fifth century BCE, does not mention them either. The accounts we have were written centuries later by writers who had probably never seen them.","In the 1990s, the British scholar Stephanie Dalley proposed a different theory. She argued that the gardens were actually built in Nineveh, the capital of the Assyrian Empire, about three hundred and fifty kilometres north of Babylon, by King Sennacherib about a century earlier. Assyrian records describe a magnificent palace garden at Nineveh, watered by a system of canals and aqueducts, and a carving from the period appears to show trees growing on terraces. Dalley suggested that later writers confused the two cities.","The debate has not been settled. Some scholars find Dalley's theory convincing, while others believe that the gardens may have been a legend, inspired by real royal gardens but exaggerated over time. Whatever the truth, the story continues to capture the imagination as a symbol of human creativity in a harsh environment."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Why are the Hanging Gardens described as mysterious?","o":["They were destroyed by an earthquake.","No definite trace of them has ever been found.","They still stand in Iraq.","They were built in secret."],"k":1,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 1 explains this.","h":"لم يُعثر على أثر لها."},{"n":22,"s":"According to the famous version, why were the gardens built?","o":["to remind the king's wife of her green homeland","to grow food for the city","to impress Greek visitors","to protect the palace from floods"],"k":0,"ty":"purpose","e":"Paragraph 2 explains this.","h":"لتذكير الملكة بموطنها."},{"n":23,"s":"The phrase 'like the seats of a theatre' describes","o":["the size of the audience","the colour of the flowers","the shape of the river","the way the gardens rose in layers"],"k":3,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"The gardens rose in layers.","h":"المدرجات."},{"n":24,"s":"What would have been an extraordinary engineering achievement?","o":["building the city walls","carving stone statues","crossing the desert","lifting water to the top of the gardens"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 3 describes the irrigation system.","h":"رفع المياه."},{"n":25,"s":"Which evidence suggests the gardens may not have been in Babylon?","o":["Archaeologists found them in Egypt.","Babylonian records and Herodotus do not mention them.","The king had no wife.","The River Euphrates was too far away."],"k":1,"ty":"claim / evidence","e":"Paragraph 4 lists the missing evidence.","h":"غياب ذكرها في السجلات."},{"n":26,"s":"What is the main purpose of paragraph 4?","o":["to describe the gardens' plants","to explain how Herodotus travelled","to praise Nebuchadnezzar","to present problems with the traditional story"],"k":3,"ty":"insertion / paragraph function","e":"It begins 'there are serious problems with this story'.","h":"عرض مشكلات الرواية."},{"n":27,"s":"According to Stephanie Dalley, where were the gardens actually built?","o":["in Giza","in Nineveh","in Babylon","in Athens"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 5 explains her theory.","h":"في نينوى."},{"n":28,"s":"What does Dalley suggest happened to the story?","o":["Later writers confused Nineveh with Babylon.","Herodotus invented it.","Sennacherib destroyed the evidence.","The gardens were moved to Babylon."],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"'later writers confused the two cities'.","h":"الخلط بين المدينتين."},{"n":29,"s":"What is the writer's position on the debate?","o":["Dalley is definitely right.","It remains unresolved.","The gardens definitely existed in Babylon.","The question is not important."],"k":1,"ty":"attitude / tone","e":"'The debate has not been settled.'","h":"لم يُحسم."},{"n":30,"s":"How is the passage organized?","o":["It lists the Seven Wonders in order.","It describes a journey to Iraq.","It compares two kings' lives.","It presents the traditional story, then questions it and offers an alternative theory."],"k":3,"ty":"organization","e":"Story → problems → new theory → conclusion.","h":"رواية ثم تشكيك ثم نظرية بديلة."}]},{"t":"Memory and multitasking","p":["Many people are proud of their ability to multitask: replying to messages while watching a lecture, listening to music while studying or checking emails during a meeting. In a world full of digital devices, doing several things at once seems efficient and even necessary. However, research in psychology and neuroscience suggests that multitasking may harm our ability to concentrate, learn and remember.","The first problem is that the human brain cannot truly focus on two demanding tasks at the same time. What we call multitasking is usually 'task switching': rapidly moving attention from one task to another. Each switch has a small cost. The brain needs time to stop thinking about one task and to restart the other. These delays, called switch costs, may last only a fraction of a second, but when they are repeated many times, they can significantly reduce productivity and increase mistakes.","Multitasking also affects memory. To remember information, we must first pay attention to it and then process it deeply enough for it to be stored. When attention is divided, information is processed less thoroughly. In one study, students who used their laptops for unrelated activities during a lecture scored lower on a test of the lecture content than students who did not. Surprisingly, students sitting near the multitaskers also scored lower, probably because the screens distracted them.","Some research suggests that people who often use several media at the same time may become worse at filtering out irrelevant information. In experiments, heavy media multitaskers were more easily distracted by unimportant details than light multitaskers. However, scientists are still debating whether multitasking causes these differences or whether people who are easily distracted are simply more likely to multitask.","Not all combinations of activities are equally harmful. Tasks that are automatic, such as walking, can often be combined with other activities with little cost. Problems arise mainly when two tasks require the same mental resources, such as reading and listening to speech, or when one task is complex and important. Using a phone while driving is a dangerous example, because both activities require attention and quick reactions.","Experts recommend several strategies to improve concentration. These include turning off notifications during study sessions, working on one task for a fixed period before taking a short break, and keeping the phone in another room while studying. Such simple habits can help people learn more effectively and feel less stressed."],"q":[{"n":31,"s":"What is the main argument of the passage?","o":["Multitasking always improves productivity.","Digital devices should be banned.","Multitasking can harm concentration, learning and memory.","People cannot learn while walking."],"k":2,"ty":"main idea","e":"The passage presents research showing the costs of multitasking.","h":"تعدد المهام يضر التركيز والذاكرة."},{"n":32,"s":"According to paragraph 2, what is multitasking usually?","o":["rapidly switching attention between tasks","doing two tasks perfectly at once","focusing on one task for a long time","using two devices at the same speed"],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 2 explains 'task switching'.","h":"التنقل السريع بين المهام."},{"n":33,"s":"What are 'switch costs'?","o":["delays that occur when the brain changes from one task to another","the price of new devices","mistakes made by teachers","the cost of electricity"],"k":0,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Paragraph 2 defines them.","h":"تأخيرات التنقل."},{"n":34,"s":"Why does divided attention affect memory?","o":["The brain stops storing all information.","Memory improves with distraction.","Devices delete information.","Information is processed less deeply."],"k":3,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 3 explains this.","h":"معالجة أقل عمقًا."},{"n":35,"s":"What was surprising about the laptop study?","o":["Multitaskers scored higher.","No students used laptops.","Students near the multitaskers also scored lower.","The lecture was cancelled."],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 3 reports this.","h":"المجاورون تأثروا أيضًا."},{"n":36,"s":"What are scientists still debating, according to paragraph 4?","o":["whether multitasking causes distraction or distracted people multitask more","whether laptops are useful","whether walking is automatic","whether notifications can be turned off"],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 4 explains the debate.","h":"اتجاه السببية."},{"n":37,"s":"When is multitasking least harmful?","o":["when one task is automatic","when both tasks are complex","when reading and listening at once","when driving and using a phone"],"k":0,"ty":"inference","e":"Automatic tasks can be combined with little cost.","h":"عندما تكون المهمة تلقائية."},{"n":38,"s":"Why does the writer mention using a phone while driving?","o":["to explain how phones work","to show that driving is automatic","as a dangerous example of combining demanding tasks","to describe a new law"],"k":2,"ty":"purpose","e":"Both require attention and quick reactions.","h":"مثال خطير."},{"n":39,"s":"Which of the following is NOT recommended in the last paragraph?","o":["turning off notifications","working for a fixed period then taking a break","keeping the phone in another room","studying with music and messages at the same time"],"k":3,"ty":"NOT / EXCEPT","e":"Studying with music and messages contradicts the advice.","h":"غير موصى به."},{"n":40,"s":"Which statement is a fact rather than an opinion?","o":["Multitasking is the worst habit of modern life.","In one study, laptop multitaskers scored lower on a test.","Everyone should stop using phones.","Students who multitask are lazy."],"k":1,"ty":"fact / opinion","e":"A reported research result.","h":"نتيجة بحثية."}]}],"i":"Read each passage and answer the questions that follow. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","iar":"اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة."},{"id":"S","name":"Sentence Structure","ar":"تركيب الجمل","min":35,"from":41,"to":70,"g":[{"i":"Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","err":false,"q":[{"n":41,"s":"She looks exhausted. She ______ since six o'clock this morning.","o":["drives","is driving","drove","has been driving"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"has been driving — Duration up to now: present perfect continuous.","h":"المضارع التام المستمر."},{"n":42,"s":"The meeting room ______ at the moment, so we'll have to wait.","o":["is cleaning","cleans","has cleaned","is being cleaned"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"is being cleaned — Present continuous passive.","h":"المبني للمجهول المستمر."},{"n":43,"s":"You ______ wear a suit to the party. It's very informal.","o":["mustn't","can't","needn't","shouldn't to"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"needn't — No necessity: needn't.","h":"عدم الضرورة."},{"n":44,"s":"The day ______ I graduated was the happiest day of my life.","o":["which","where","whose","when"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"when — when for time.","h":"when للزمن."},{"n":45,"s":"If she spoke Spanish, she ______ the job in Madrid.","o":["will get","would get","gets","would have get"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"would get — Second conditional.","h":"الشرط الثاني."},{"n":46,"s":"I'm thinking of ______ a car next year.","o":["to buy","buy","bought","buying"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"buying — Preposition + -ing.","h":"بعد of يأتي -ing."},{"n":47,"s":"Where did you have your photos ______?","o":["printed","print","printing","to print"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"printed — Causative.","h":"التركيب السببي."},{"n":48,"s":"This is by far ______ difficult exam I have ever taken.","o":["more","much more","the more","the most"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"the most — by far + superlative.","h":"by far مع التفضيل."},{"n":49,"s":"The lights are off. They ______ have gone to bed already.","o":["can't","must","needn't","shouldn't"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"must — Logical certainty about the past: must have.","h":"استنتاج يقيني."},{"n":50,"s":"I wish you ______ complaining about the weather all the time!","o":["would stop","stop","stopped yesterday","had stopped"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"would stop — Annoyance: wish + would.","h":"wish + would."},{"n":51,"s":"Next month, my grandparents ______ married for fifty years.","o":["will be being","are","have been","will have been"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"will have been — Future perfect with duration.","h":"المستقبل التام."},{"n":52,"s":"The manager wanted to know when we ______ the project.","o":["will finish","finish","would finish","have finished"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"would finish — Reported question: will → would.","h":"الكلام المنقول."},{"n":53,"s":"______ it was expensive, the hotel was not very comfortable.","o":["Despite","In spite of","Although","Because"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"Although — Contrast clause: Although.","h":"Although."},{"n":54,"s":"There was ______ traffic that we missed our flight.","o":["such","so much","so many","too much"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"so much — so much + uncountable noun + that.","h":"so much."},{"n":55,"s":"Mathematics ______ my favourite subject when I was at school.","o":["was","were","have been","are"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"was — Mathematics takes a singular verb.","h":"Mathematics مفرد."},{"n":56,"s":"He ______ to living in a hot climate after a few months.","o":["used","got used","was use","uses"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"got used — get used to + -ing.","h":"get used to."},{"n":57,"s":"The students, most of ______ were from abroad, enjoyed the trip.","o":["who","them","whom","which"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"whom — most of whom in a non-defining clause.","h":"most of whom."},{"n":58,"s":"Seldom ______ such an amazing performance.","o":["have we seen","we have seen","we saw","seen we have"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"have we seen — Negative adverb at the start: inversion.","h":"القلب بعد Seldom."},{"n":59,"s":"She managed ______ the exam despite being ill.","o":["passing","to pass","pass","passed"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"to pass — manage + to + verb.","h":"manage + to."},{"n":60,"s":"But for the rescue team, the climbers ______.","o":["would die","would have died","died","had died"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"would have died — But for + past unreal result.","h":"But for."}]},{"i":"Choose the underlined part (A, B, C or D) that is incorrect.","err":true,"q":[{"n":61,"s":"The (A) amount of cars on the roads (B) is (C) increasing (D) rapidly.","o":["amount","is","increasing","rapidly"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"amount — cars is countable: The number of.","h":"number مع المعدود."},{"n":62,"s":"If he (A) had (B) practised more, he (C) would win the match (D) last week.","o":["had","practised","would win","last"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"would win — Third conditional: would have won.","h":"would have won."},{"n":63,"s":"My sister (A) is (B) interesting (C) in (D) history.","o":["is","interesting","in","history"],"k":1,"ty":"error identification","e":"interesting — She feels the interest: interested.","h":"interested."},{"n":64,"s":"They (A) have (B) went to the (C) museum (D) twice this month.","o":["have","went","museum","twice"],"k":1,"ty":"error identification","e":"went — Present perfect: have gone / been.","h":"التصريف الثالث."},{"n":65,"s":"Neither the teacher nor the students (A) knew (B) where the (C) keys (D) was.","o":["knew","where","keys","was"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"was — the keys is plural: were.","h":"keys جمع: were."},{"n":66,"s":"(A) Despite she was tired, (B) she (C) finished (D) her work.","o":["Despite","she","finished","her"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"Despite — A clause needs Although.","h":"Although مع الجملة."},{"n":67,"s":"(A) Every of the (B) rooms (C) has a (D) balcony.","o":["Every","rooms","has","balcony"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"Every — Every cannot be followed by of: Each of.","h":"Each of."},{"n":68,"s":"The man (A) whose car (B) was stolen (C) have reported (D) it to the police.","o":["whose","was","have","it"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"have — The man is singular: has.","h":"الفاعل مفرد: has."},{"n":69,"s":"She (A) asked me (B) if I (C) had ever (D) visit Japan.","o":["asked","if","had","visit"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"visit — Past perfect: had visited.","h":"التصريف الثالث."},{"n":70,"s":"Seldom (A) have I (B) seen such a (C) beautifully (D) view.","o":["have","seen","beautifully","view"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"beautifully — An adjective is needed before a noun: beautiful.","h":"الصفة: beautiful."}]}],"iar":"الأسئلة من ٤١ إلى ٦٠: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."},{"id":"L","name":"Listening Comprehension","ar":"فهم المسموع","min":30,"from":71,"to":90,"g":[{"rec":1,"a":"M16-L-01","q":[{"n":71,"s":"What must the student do to avoid the penalty?","o":["submit a new assignment","show the lecturer the repair receipt","pay a fine","write an extra essay"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"'if you can show me the repair receipt, I won't apply the penalty.'","h":"إظهار إيصال الإصلاح."}],"t":"A late assignment and a penalty","sc":["Situation: A student speaks to her lecturer. (70 words)","Woman: Dr. Faisal, I submitted my assignment two days late because my laptop broke. Will I lose marks?","Man: Normally, students lose ten per cent for each day late. But if you can show me the repair receipt, I won't apply the penalty.","Woman: I have the receipt from the shop. I'll email you a copy today.","Man: That's fine. Next time, please save your work online as well, so you have a backup."]},{"rec":2,"a":"M16-L-02","q":[{"n":72,"s":"Who was responsible for the mistake?","o":["the customer","the delivery driver","the printing company","the bride's family"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"'the mistake was ours'.","h":"الشركة."}],"t":"A misprinted wedding invitation","sc":["Situation: A man calls a printing company. (59 words)","Man: Hello. I collected my wedding invitations yesterday, but the date is wrong. It says the twelfth instead of the twenty-first.","Woman: I'm very sorry. Let me check your order. Yes, the mistake was ours. You wrote twenty-first on the form.","Man: I need to send them out this week.","Woman: We'll reprint them free of charge, and they'll be ready tomorrow afternoon."]},{"rec":3,"a":"M16-L-03","q":[{"n":73,"s":"Why does the woman need the car moved?","o":["She wants to wash her car.","She has to take her son to a hospital appointment.","She is going to work late.","Her brother is visiting."],"k":1,"ty":"reason","e":"She needs to take her son to the hospital.","h":"موعد المستشفى."}],"t":"Asking a neighbour to move a car","sc":["Situation: A woman knocks on her neighbour's door early in the morning. (63 words)","Woman: Good morning. I'm sorry to disturb you so early, but your car is blocking my garage, and I need to take my son to the hospital for an appointment.","Man: Oh, I'm so sorry. My brother parked it there last night when he visited. I'll move it right away.","Woman: Thank you. It's quite urgent.","Man: Of course. Give me one minute to find the keys."]},{"rec":4,"a":"M16-L-04","q":[{"n":74,"s":"What does the waiter offer as an apology?","o":["a free main course","a free dessert","a discount on the bill","a different table"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"'dessert will be on us tonight'.","h":"حلوى مجانية."}],"t":"A complaint about cold food","sc":["Situation: A customer speaks to a waiter. (53 words)","Man: Excuse me, my soup is cold, and the rice is not very warm either.","Man: I'm terribly sorry, sir. The kitchen has been very busy tonight. I'll take it back and bring you a fresh, hot meal.","Man: Thank you. I'd also like some extra bread, please.","Man: Certainly. And dessert will be on us tonight."]},{"rec":5,"a":"M16-L-05","q":[{"n":75,"s":"When must the woman return the lens?","o":["on Sunday evening","on Sunday morning","next week","on Saturday night"],"k":3,"ty":"correction","e":"'could you bring it back on Saturday night?'","h":"ليلة السبت."}],"t":"Borrowing a camera lens","sc":["Situation: Two friends who enjoy photography are talking. (56 words)","Woman: Could I borrow your wide-angle lens this weekend? I'm photographing the old buildings in Al-Balad.","Woman: Sure, but be careful. It was very expensive. I'll put it in its protective case.","Woman: Of course. I'll return it on Sunday evening.","Woman: Actually, could you bring it back on Saturday night? I need it for a wedding on Sunday morning."]},{"rec":6,"a":"M16-L-06","q":[{"n":76,"s":"What is the station doing to help passengers?","o":["adding extra carriages to the later train","providing free buses","offering free meals","delaying all trains"],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"'We're adding extra carriages'.","h":"إضافة عربات."}],"t":"A cancelled train","sc":["Situation: A passenger speaks to a station employee. (56 words)","Man: The screen says the four o'clock train to Riyadh is cancelled. What happened?","Woman: There's a technical problem with the train. Passengers can take the five thirty train instead, or we can give you a full refund.","Man: Will the five thirty train be very crowded?","Woman: We're adding extra carriages, so there should be enough seats for everyone."]},{"rec":7,"a":"M16-L-07","q":[{"n":77,"s":"When will the call take place?","o":["on Tuesday at ten","on Wednesday after two","on Thursday morning","on Wednesday at eleven"],"k":3,"ty":"correction","e":"'Then let's say Wednesday at eleven.'","h":"الأربعاء الحادية عشرة."}],"t":"Choosing a time for a group call","sc":["Situation: Three colleagues in different cities are arranging a call. (47 words)","Man: We need to have a video call this week. Is Tuesday at ten good for everyone?","Woman: I'm visiting a client on Tuesday morning. What about Wednesday?","Man: Wednesday morning is fine for me, but I'm busy after two.","Man: Then let's say Wednesday at eleven. I'll send the link."]},{"rec":8,"a":"M16-L-08","q":[{"n":78,"s":"Why will the security officer cancel the old card?","o":["because it has expired","so no one else can use it","because the office is closed","because the photo is old Longer conversations"],"k":1,"ty":"purpose","e":"'so no one else can use it'.","h":"حتى لا يستخدمها غيرها."}],"t":"A lost access card at work","sc":["Situation: An employee speaks to the security office. (57 words)","Woman: Hi. I've lost my access card, and I can't get into the office.","Man: No problem. I'll cancel the old card so no one else can use it, and I'll give you a temporary card for today.","Woman: When will my new card be ready?","Man: Tomorrow morning. You'll need to come here to collect it and sign the form."]},{"rec":9,"a":"M16-L-09","q":[{"n":79,"s":"Why does the second teacher want to include some lessons?","o":["so that the visit is not just a holiday","because the Jordanian school requested it","because the museum is closed","because parents complained"],"k":0,"ty":"purpose","e":"'so it isn't just a holiday'.","h":"حتى لا تكون مجرد عطلة."},{"n":80,"s":"What will the mixed groups of students do?","o":["visit Amman together","cook traditional food","prepare a presentation comparing the two countries","write letters to parents"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"'work in mixed groups on a presentation comparing the two countries'.","h":"عرض مقارن."}],"t":"Planning an exchange visit with a school in Jordan","sc":["Situation: Two teachers are planning a student exchange. (144 words)","Woman: The exchange visit with the school in Amman is confirmed for March. Fifteen of their students will stay with our students' families for a week.","Woman: Wonderful. We need to plan activities that show them our culture and history.","Woman: I thought we could take them to Diriyah and the National Museum on the first two days.","Woman: Good. And we should include some lessons, so it isn't just a holiday. Maybe they could join our science and English classes.","Woman: Yes. And what about a joint project? Our students and theirs could work in mixed groups on a presentation comparing the two countries.","Woman: That's an excellent idea. They'd present it at a closing ceremony for parents.","Woman: We also need to choose host families carefully. Each family must agree to collect their guest from school every day.","Woman: I'll send a letter to parents this week to find volunteers."]},{"rec":10,"a":"M16-L-10","q":[{"n":81,"s":"Why might the club be unable to go on the AlUla trip?","o":["Its budget has been reduced.","The trip is too dangerous.","Members are too busy.","The university has banned trips."],"k":0,"ty":"reason","e":"The budget was cut by thirty per cent.","h":"تقليص الميزانية."},{"n":82,"s":"Why shouldn't the trip fee be too high?","o":["Sponsors will pay everything.","The university does not allow fees.","Some members cannot afford much.","The trip is very short."],"k":2,"ty":"reason","e":"Some members are on scholarships.","h":"بعض الأعضاء لا يستطيعون الدفع."}],"t":"Discussing changes to a club budget","sc":["Situation: Two members of a university photography club are talking. (150 words)","Man: The university has cut our club budget by thirty per cent this year.","Man: That's a big cut. We won't be able to afford the trip to AlUla.","Man: Maybe we can still go if we find sponsors. A local camera shop might pay part of the cost in exchange for advertising.","Man: Good idea. We could also charge members a small fee for the trip.","Man: Yes, but not too much. Some members are on scholarships and can't pay much.","Man: What about selling prints of our best photos at the university exhibition?","Man: That could work. Last year, people asked if they could buy them.","Man: I'll contact the camera shop tomorrow. Can you organize the exhibition sales?","Man: Sure. I'll ask the art department if we can use their printers. If we sell fifty prints, that could cover almost half the cost of the trip.","Man: Then let's choose our best photos at the next meeting."]},{"rec":11,"a":"M16-L-11","q":[{"n":83,"s":"Why does the student choose programming?","o":["She has a lot of programming experience.","Her friends are taking it.","It is the cheapest programme.","It will be useful for her engineering studies."],"k":3,"ty":"reason","e":"She plans to study engineering, so programming is more useful.","h":"مفيدة لدراسة الهندسة."},{"n":84,"s":"Why is the introductory group suitable for her?","o":["It is for advanced students.","It is taught online.","She has never written code, and it ends before the family trip.","It includes creative writing. Talks and lectures"],"k":2,"ty":"inference","e":"She is a beginner, and it finishes before the trip.","h":"مناسبة للمبتدئين وتنتهي قبل الرحلة."}],"t":"Choosing a programme for a summer school","sc":["Situation: A student talks to her mother about summer programmes. (142 words)","Woman: Mum, the university is offering three summer programmes for high school students: creative writing, computer programming and environmental science.","Woman: Which one interests you most?","Woman: I love writing, but I'm planning to study engineering at university.","Woman: Then programming might be more useful for your future.","Woman: That's what I was thinking. But the programming course is full of advanced students, and I've never written any code.","Woman: Is there a beginners' group?","Woman: Yes, there's an introductory group that starts a week earlier. It finishes before our family trip in August.","Woman: Perfect. You can still write stories in your free time, and perhaps you could join the creative writing programme next summer instead.","Woman: Good idea. I'll register for the introductory programming group online tonight, before the places are all taken.","Woman: Don't forget to ask whether they provide laptops, or whether you need to bring your own."]},{"rec":12,"a":"M16-L-12","q":[{"n":85,"s":"What is an atoll?","o":["a ring of coral islands around a lagoon","an active volcano","a deep ocean trench","a type of sea animal"],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"The lecturer defines it.","h":"حلقة جزر مرجانية."},{"n":86,"s":"Why do the corals keep growing upwards?","o":["They are pushed by the waves.","The volcano lifts them.","They avoid predators.","They need sunlight to survive."],"k":3,"ty":"reason","e":"Algae inside them need sunlight.","h":"تحتاج الضوء."},{"n":87,"s":"How did scientists confirm Darwin's theory?","o":["by watching a volcano sink","by finding volcanic rock deep under the coral","by measuring sea levels","by counting coral species"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"Drilling found volcanic rock over a kilometre below.","h":"بالحفر."}],"t":"Lecture: how coral islands form","sc":["Situation: A marine science lecturer is speaking to students. (251 words)","Lecturer: Good morning. Today we'll look at how coral islands, also known as atolls, are formed. An atoll is a ring-shaped island or chain of islands made of coral, surrounding a shallow lagoon. Many atolls are found in the Pacific and Indian Oceans, such as the Maldives. The first person to explain how they form was Charles Darwin, in the nineteenth century, and his theory is still accepted today. The process begins with a volcanic island in a warm, tropical sea. Corals, which are tiny animals that build hard skeletons of calcium carbonate, begin to grow in the shallow water around the island's coast, forming a fringing reef. Over millions of years, the volcano stops erupting, and the island slowly begins to sink because the ocean floor beneath it cools and becomes heavier. As the island sinks, the corals keep growing upwards towards the sunlight, which they need to survive because tiny algae live inside them and produce food through photosynthesis. Eventually, the volcanic island disappears completely beneath the surface, but the ring of coral remains at sea level, surrounding a lagoon where the island used to be. Waves break pieces of coral and pile up sand on the reef, creating low islands where plants can grow. Scientists confirmed Darwin's theory in the twentieth century by drilling through coral on Pacific atolls and finding volcanic rock more than a kilometre below. Today, atolls are in danger from rising sea levels, because most of them are only a few metres above the water."]},{"rec":13,"a":"M16-L-13","q":[{"n":88,"s":"What do ground controllers do?","o":["follow planes across the country","fly the aircraft","repair radar screens","guide aircraft between the gates and the runways"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Ground controllers guide aircraft on the ground.","h":"توجيه الطائرات على الأرض."},{"n":89,"s":"Why are clear, short instructions essential?","o":["Pilots speak different languages.","Radio time is expensive.","Misunderstandings can be dangerous.","Controllers are very busy."],"k":2,"ty":"reason","e":"'misunderstandings can be dangerous'.","h":"سوء الفهم خطير."},{"n":90,"s":"Why do controllers take regular breaks?","o":["The work is very intense.","The airport closes every two hours.","Their screens need cooling.","Pilots change every two hours."],"k":0,"ty":"reason","e":"'Because the work is so intense, controllers take regular breaks'.","h":"العمل مكثف."}],"t":"Talk: the work of air traffic controllers","sc":["Situation: An air traffic controller speaks to visitors at an airport. (251 words)","Lecturer: Welcome to the control tower. My job is to help aircraft move safely and efficiently, both on the ground and in the air. At a busy airport like this one, a plane may take off or land every two minutes, so our work requires constant concentration. Air traffic control is usually divided into several areas. Ground controllers guide aircraft as they move between the gates and the runways, making sure they do not collide with other planes or vehicles. Tower controllers, like me, give permission for take-offs and landings and keep aircraft at safe distances near the airport. Once a plane has climbed away from the airport, it is handed over to area controllers in another centre, who use radar to follow it across the country. We communicate with pilots by radio, using standard phrases in English, which is the international language of aviation. Clear, short instructions are essential, because misunderstandings can be dangerous. We also use radar screens and computer systems that show each aircraft's position, height, speed and identity. To become an air traffic controller, people need excellent concentration, a good memory and the ability to make quick decisions under pressure. Training is long and demanding, and controllers must pass regular medical and skills tests. Because the work is so intense, controllers take regular breaks, usually after no more than two hours at a screen. It's a stressful job, but it's also very rewarding to know that you are helping thousands of passengers reach their destinations safely every day."]}],"i":"You will hear 13 recordings: 8 short conversations (one question each), 3 longer conversations (two questions each) and 2 talks (three questions each). Read the questions before each recording, then choose the best answer.","iar":"ستسمع ثلاثة عشر تسجيلًا: ثماني محادثات قصيرة (سؤال لكل منها)، وثلاث محادثات أطول (سؤالان لكل منها)، وحديثين أو محاضرتين (ثلاثة أسئلة لكل منهما). اقرأ الأسئلة قبل بدء كل تسجيل."},{"id":"C","name":"Composition Analysis","ar":"التحليل الإنشائي","min":20,"from":91,"to":100,"g":[{"q":[{"n":91,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) As a result, many young people now see farming as a modern career.","(2) Traditional farming in Saudi Arabia faced many challenges, such as water shortages.","(3) In recent years, however, new technologies have been introduced.","(4) Greenhouses, drip irrigation and sensors now allow farmers to grow more with less water."],"k":2,"ty":"best order","e":"problem → however, new tech → examples → result.","h":"تسلسل منطقي."},{"n":92,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Moreover","Therefore","However","For example"],"x":["The new library is spacious and modern. ______, it has very few books in English."],"k":2,"ty":"transition / connector","e":"A contrast between positive and negative points.","h":"تضاد."},{"n":93,"s":"Each of the (A) candidates (B) were asked to (C) give a short (D) presentation.","o":["candidates","were","give","presentation"],"k":1,"ty":"error","e":"Each of … takes a singular verb: was.","h":"Each مفرد."},{"n":94,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Camels are well adapted to desert life. (2) Their humps store fat, which provides energy when food is scarce. (3) They can close their nostrils to keep out sand. (4) Horses were used by many ancient armies. (5) Their thick lips allow them to eat thorny plants."],"k":3,"ty":"irrelevant sentence","e":"Horses in ancient armies are not about camels' adaptations.","h":"الخيول خارج الموضوع."},{"n":95,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["As a result","Nevertheless","On the other hand","In contrast"],"x":["The company's new product was very popular. ______, its profits doubled within a year."],"k":0,"ty":"transition / connector","e":"Doubled profits are a result.","h":"النتيجة."},{"n":96,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) Finally, the results are analysed and published in a report.","(2) Conducting a survey involves several stages.","(3) First, researchers design clear questions.","(4) Then, they collect answers from a large group of people."],"k":2,"ty":"best order","e":"topic → First → Then → Finally.","h":"ترتيب المراحل."},{"n":97,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Technology has made it easier for families to stay in touch.","Messages can be very short.","Some families live in different countries.","Video calls need a camera."],"x":["______ It takes only a few seconds to send a message to someone on the other side of the world, and video calls allow families to see each other every day."],"k":0,"ty":"topic sentence / thesis","e":"The details show how technology connects families.","h":"التقنية تقرّب العائلات."},{"n":98,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Students should therefore make time for reading every day.","Some books are very long.","Libraries are quiet places.","Many students prefer films."],"x":["Regular reading has many benefits for students. It improves vocabulary, strengthens writing skills and increases general knowledge. It can also reduce stress and improve concentration. ______"],"k":0,"ty":"concluding sentence","e":"A recommendation that follows from the benefits.","h":"توصية."},{"n":99,"s":"The research (A) shows that people who (B) exercises regularly (C) sleep (D) better.","o":["shows","exercises","sleep","better"],"k":1,"ty":"error","e":"people is plural: exercise.","h":"people جمع: exercise."},{"n":100,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Astronauts train for many years.","The Moon is about 384,000 kilometres away.","Some rockets are very tall.","At present, a trip into space costs millions of dollars. Teacher Section — Mock 16"],"x":["Many people dream of travelling into space. ______ In the future, however, space tourism may become more affordable."],"k":3,"ty":"complete the paragraph","e":"However contrasts the present cost with the future.","h":"التكلفة الحالية قبل However."}]}],"i":"Read each paragraph or set of sentences and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","iar":"اقرأ كل فقرة أو مجموعة جمل واختر الإجابة الصحيحة."}]};
